a-aʿriḍū","verse_key":"4:16"},{"pos":9,"ar":"عَنْهُمَآ ۗ","en_gloss":"from both of them","transliteration":"ʿanhumā","verse_key":"4:16"},{"pos":10,"ar":"إِنَّ","en_gloss":"Indeed","transliteration":"inna","verse_key":"4:16"},{"pos":11,"ar":"ٱللَّهَ","en_gloss":"Allah","transliteration":"l-laha","verse_key":"4:16"},{"pos":12,"ar":"كَانَ","en_gloss":"is","transliteration":"kāna","verse_key":"4:16"},{"pos":13,"ar":"تَوَّابًۭا","en_gloss":"Oft-Forgiving","transliteration":"tawwāban","verse_key":"4:16"},{"pos":14,"ar":"رَّحِيمًا","en_gloss":"Most-Merciful","transliteration":"raḥīman","verse_key":"4:16"},{"pos":15,"ar":"١٦","en_gloss":"(16)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"4:16"}]},{"verse_key":"4:17","surah":4,"ayah":17,"ar_uthmani":"إِنَّمَا ٱلتَّوْبَةُ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ لِلَّذِينَ يَعْمَلُونَ ٱلسُّوٓءَ بِجَهَـٰلَةٍ ثُمَّ يَتُوبُونَ مِن قَرِيبٍ فَأُو۟لَـٰٓئِكَ يَتُوبُ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيْهِمْ ۗ وَكَانَ ٱللَّهُ عَلِيمًا حَكِيمًا","en_translation_id":85,"en":"But God only undertakes to accept repentance from those who do evil out of ignorance and soon afterwards repent: these are the ones God will forgive, He is all knowing, all wise.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"إِنَّمَا","en_gloss":"Only","transliteration":"innamā","verse_key":"4:17"},{"pos":2,"ar":"ٱلتَّوْبَةُ","en_gloss":"the acceptance of repentance","transliteration":"l-tawbatu","verse_key":"4:17"},{"pos":3,"ar":"عَلَى","en_gloss":"by","transliteration":"ʿalā","verse_key":"4:17"},{"pos":4,"ar":"ٱللَّهِ","en_gloss":"Allah","transliteration":"l-lahi","verse_key":"4:17"},{"pos":5,"ar":"لِلَّذِينَ","en_gloss":"(is) for those who","transliteration":"lilladhīna","verse_key":"4:17"},{"pos":6,"ar":"يَعْمَلُونَ","en_gloss":"do","transliteration":"yaʿmalūna","verse_key":"4:17"},{"pos":7,"ar":"ٱلسُّوٓءَ","en_gloss":"the evil","transliteration":"l-sūa","verse_key":"4:17"},{"pos":8,"ar":"بِجَهَـٰلَةٍۢ","en_gloss":"in ignorance","transliteration":"bijahālatin","verse_key":"4:17"},{"pos":9,"ar":"ثُمَّ","en_gloss":"then","transliteration":"thumma","verse_key":"4:17"},{"pos":10,"ar":"يَتُوبُونَ","en_gloss":"they repent","transliteration":"yatūbūna","verse_key":"4:17"},{"pos":11,"ar":"مِن","en_gloss":"from","transliteration":"min","verse_key":"4:17"},{"pos":12,"ar":"قَرِيبٍۢ","en_gloss":"soon after","transliteration":"qarībin","verse_key":"4:17"},{"pos":13,"ar":"فَأُو۟لَـٰٓئِكَ","en_gloss":"Then those","transliteration":"fa-ulāika","verse_key":"4:17"},{"pos":14,"ar":"يَتُوبُ","en_gloss":"will have forgiveness","transliteration":"yatūbu","verse_key":"4:17"},{"pos":15,"ar":"ٱللَّهُ","en_gloss":"(from) Allah","transliteration":"l-lahu","verse_key":"4:17"},{"pos":16,"ar":"عَلَيْهِمْ ۗ","en_gloss":"upon them","transliteration":"ʿalayhim","verse_key":"4:17"},{"pos":17,"ar":"وَكَانَ","en_gloss":"and is","transliteration":"wakāna","verse_key":"4:17"},{"pos":18,"ar":"ٱللَّهُ","en_gloss":"Allah","transliteration":"l-lahu","verse_key":"4:17"},{"pos":19,"ar":"عَلِيمًا","en_gloss":"All-Knowing","transliteration":"ʿalīman","verse_key":"4:17"},{"pos":20,"ar":"حَكِيمًۭا","en_gloss":"All-Wise","transliteration":"ḥakīman","verse_key":"4:17"},{"pos":21,"ar":"١٧","en_gloss":"(17)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"4:17"}]},{"verse_key":"4:18","surah":4,"ayah":18,"ar_uthmani":"وَلَيْسَتِ ٱلتَّوْبَةُ لِلَّذِينَ يَعْمَلُونَ ٱلسَّيِّـَٔاتِ حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا حَضَرَ أَحَدَهُمُ ٱلْمَوْتُ قَالَ إِنِّى تُبْتُ ٱلْـَٔـٰنَ وَلَا ٱلَّذِينَ يَمُوتُونَ وَهُمْ كُفَّارٌ ۚ أُو۟لَـٰٓئِكَ أَعْتَدْنَا لَهُمْ عَذَابًا أَلِيمًا","en_translation_id":85,"en":"It is not true repentance when people continue to do evil until death confronts them and then say, ‘Now I repent,’ nor when they die defiant: We have prepared a painful torment for these.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"وَلَيْسَتِ","en_gloss":"And not","transliteration":"walaysati","verse_key":"4:18"},{"pos":2,"ar":"ٱلتَّوْبَةُ","en_gloss":"(is) the acceptance of repentance","transliteration":"l-tawbatu","verse_key":"4:18"},{"pos":3,"ar":"لِلَّذِينَ","en_gloss":"for those who","transliteration":"lilladhī